  THE ENTRY POINT, REBUILT FROM THE IONISATION ENERGIES

  a_meas = (n - nu) / sqrt(p),  nu = sqrt(R / IE),  p = n - l - 1

  1. REGISTER 1334, the 3p filling at constant n, l and p
     el     IE (eV)       nu   a_meas   printed
     Al      5.9858   1.5076   1.4924   1.49   agrees
     Si      8.1517   1.2919   1.7081   1.71   agrees
     P      10.4867   1.1390   1.8610   1.86   agrees
     S      10.3600   1.1460   1.8540   1.85   agrees
     Cl     12.9676   1.0243   1.9757   1.98   agrees
     Ar     15.7596   0.9292   2.0708   2.07   agrees
     Six of six.  a_meas rises as the subshell fills, which is register 1334's
     point: nu depends on OCCUPANCY and the law has no coordinate for it.

  2. REGISTER 1337, t at the opening
     sub  el     a_meas          L          U        t   printed
     3p   Al     1.4924  0.0000000  1.3660254   1.0925   1.0925   agrees
     4p   Ga     1.7636  0.0000000  1.7071068   1.0331   1.0331   agrees
